course: dictionary
lesson: 2921
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Drama is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask which meaning fits. «Chloe joined drama club this term.» Here drama club is a club for acting and performing, so drama means the school subject of acting.
explain: «A TV drama» is a serious show that actors perform on television. The clues are TV and show, so drama means a play for TV, not a school lesson. Always test your meaning: put it in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes drama means fuss. «Stop the drama, it's only a lost pencil.» Nobody is acting here. People are making a big scene over something small, so drama means unnecessary arguing or gossip. Someone who overreacts like this is called a drama queen.
fact: Drama can mean a play for the theatre, TV or radio, a story acted out by people.
fact: Drama can also mean the school subject of acting, voice and movement, as in «drama class» or «drama club».
fact: Drama can mean an exciting, unusual or upsetting event or situation.
fact: Informally, drama means unnecessary fuss, arguing or gossip, as in «I don't want any drama.»
fact: Some phrases use drama in special ways: «drama queen» means someone who overreacts, and «no drama» means no problem in Australia.
exercise: «Chloe's first drama club» is at school on Tuesdays. What does drama mean here? | *A subject for acting and performing | A loud argument | A type of dance | A thunderstorm
exercise: «If someone keeps taking your answers or ideas, a teacher can help without a big drama.» What does drama mean here? | *Unnecessary fuss | A lesson in the classroom | An exciting event | A play on the stage
exercise: «The drama was on TV last night.» What kind of drama is this? | A club for acting | Unnecessary gossip | A school lesson | *A serious series or play for television
test: «The drama was about a family that lost its home.» Which meaning fits best? | A school subject for acting | Unnecessary fuss | *A play acted out for TV or the theatre | A thunderstorm
test: Ruby says, «Don't make a drama out of it!» What does make a drama out of it mean? | *Make a big fuss over something small | Write a song about it | Act out a play about it | Tell a joke about it
exam: Which phrase means someone who overreacts and makes a fuss? | Drama club | TV drama | *Drama queen | Drama class
